            <ArticleTitle>[Disturbances of consciousness of old people from internal view (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Any unconsciousness and especially that of old people refers to direct danger to life and requires immediate medical intervening. A diagnostic plan will not be adequate in association to the multifariour etiological factors and can delay in a special case the beginning of an aimed therapy. The unconscious patient must have a clinical treatment. The author describes the diagnostic of the most important comatose states in the age.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
